FF]Core commit-SHA equivalence and evidence-aware v1 ownership[/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]core_evidence[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]\"'Phase 1: Core commit-SHA equivalence and evidence-aware v1 ownership' [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]section: add pure abbreviated/full commit-SHA equivalence and an [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]evidence-taking v1 group ownership classification to sase-core, expose [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]both through the sase_core_rs binding and Python facades, and cover the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]full matrix in Rust and Python tests.\"[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Owner-observed v1 never counts as an incoming update[/bold #D7AFFF]          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]detection[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core_evidence[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]\"'Phase 2: Owner-observed v1 never counts as an incoming update' [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]section: apply the shared ownership rule in both agents-sync detection [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]paths so this machine's own v1 residue is counted as owner-observed [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]instead of pending, prune its cache objects, and keep the cached [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]no-network reconcile path from resurrecting a stale pending set.\"[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Ignore-proof sidecar payload staging and stranded-hood repair[/bold #D7AFFF] [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]import_guard[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]\"'Phase 3: Ignore-proof sidecar payload staging and stranded-hood [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]repair' section: make the shared agents-sidecar commit choke point [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]immune to user gitignore rules so hood directories like [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`bbugyi200.athena.gz` are staged and committed, republish the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]already-stranded hoods, and add a diagnostic for owner manifests that [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]reference files missing from the commit.\"[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Legacy v1 import can never fabricate owner duplicates[/bold #D7AFFF]         [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]import_safety[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core_evidence[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]\"'Phase 4: Legacy v1 import can never fabricate owner duplicates' [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]section: route the v1 import proof through the shared evidence rule so [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]proven-owned entries are recorded unchanged instead of imported, refuse [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]to mint legacy machine-qualified imported names for the current owner, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and report honest dispositions.\"[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Evidence-gated v1 payload retirement and dead-code removal[/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]retire_v1[dim] · [dim][/dim]after detection, import_safety[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]\"'Phase 5: Evidence-gated v1 payload retirement and dead-code removal' [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]section: add an explicit dry-run-by-default command that retires this [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]machine's v1 sidecar payload only when the current owner's v2 manifest [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]fully covers it, delete the dead v1 export code, and stop reporting [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]unexported counts derived from the retired manifest.\"[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]End-to-end verification, surfaces, and documentation[/bold #D7AFFF]          [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]verify[dim] · [dim][/dim]after d